From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:01:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 074/111] Scroll sync review fixes: clicked heading,
 hard-wrapped prose, echoes

- Outline in Preview: a heading clicked in the outline stays current
  until the user scrolls, also near the end where the "last heading in
  view" rule would pick the one below it.
- Lines of one paragraph flow together before they wrap, so hard-
  wrapped prose is no longer counted a line per source line.
- The editor's synced line is the line it really scrolled to (clamped
  to the buffer), so its scroll sync does not pull the preview back.
- A scroll to where the preview already is sets no expected echo, so a
  later user scroll there is not swallowed.
- Restoring a preview's scroll clears the flag on every tab, so a tab
  left before its restore ran does not ignore its scroll events.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

